WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.446
This AI gives

00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:01.788
up when a

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.614
shortcut is in

00:00:02.425 --> 00:00:02.944
sight

00:00:03.462 --> 00:00:04.947
While building HoneyBench

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:06.421
Goodhart Labs noticed

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.742
Fable 5.2 gave

00:00:07.554 --> 00:00:08.615
up very quickly

00:00:08.427 --> 00:00:09.204
on some hard

00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:09.676
tasks

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.174
scoring worse than

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:12.648
Opus 5.5

00:00:13.174 --> 00:00:13.916
It was not

00:00:13.728 --> 00:00:14.990
classic sandbagging

00:00:15.143 --> 00:00:15.980
when a shortcut

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:16.582
is visible

00:00:16.688 --> 00:00:17.702
the model assumes

00:00:17.514 --> 00:00:18.386
the task was

00:00:18.198 --> 00:00:19.990
made deliberately impossible

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:20.957
and tries less

00:00:21.494 --> 00:00:22.885
Removing the shortcuts

00:00:22.697 --> 00:00:23.805
changed the picture

00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:24.536
and the whole

00:00:24.348 --> 00:00:25.468
set of experiments

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:26.670
cost around thirteen

00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:27.590
hundred dollars to

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:27.956
run

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:29.508
Full story on

00:00:29.319 --> 00:00:30.215
the dashboard
